  "title": "Indian Rupee Depresses Amid Global Crude Prices and Geopolitical Tensions",
  "summary": "The Indian rupee fell to 94.95 against the US dollar after a sharp rise in global crude oil prices, which pushed it below its previous high. The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) stepped in to stabilize the currency, but the weakening dollar helped cushion the fall, while geopolitical tensions and rising oil prices continued to affect its value. The rupee also saw a 10 paise depreciation to 94.66 against the US dollar during early trade, reflecting rising crude oil prices and geopolitical tensions in the Middle East.",
